// Test: bugfixes/validator_rule_calls_are_checked
// Grammar: function_call (validator.each)
// Semantic: FUNC002 — stdlib-reference §15 declares `validator.each(v, rules)`
//   (validator, validator); like every §15 function its calls are checked
//   against that signature
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.184
// Expected output:
// Expected error:
//   error[FUNC002]
//   Function requires at least 2 arguments, got 1
//
// Regression: `validator.shape`, `validator.each` and `validator.merge` had
// no declaration in the type checker (and `validator.trim` / `validator.type`
// none in the global symbol table MCP `list_builtins` reads), so their calls
// were not checked: a missing argument produced invalid WASM (COM001) and a
// string passed as rules compiled.

start:
	integer v = validator.field(validator.create(), "tags")
	v = validator.each(v)
	print(validator.isOk(validator.run(v, 0)))
